SwordMan 0185: FPS overlay with named numbers (game, display, frame time, GPU, main thread CPU, 1% low)

Players read the big number as the frame rate, but it was the game frames divided by dbz3_frameskip + 1, and the Renut
renderer did not skip frames: the overlay showed half of the log's FPS. Now each number has its own name, with the
meaning of the log lines: "Game" (guest swaps a second), "Display" (frames that reach the screen, each once: PresentStats::shown; the presents
repeat the last frame at the display rate), frame time (1000 / game FPS), GPU ms per
drawn frame (rex::perf::RecordGpuFrame: Xenia from the dbz3 timestamps, the Renut from its queries), main thread CPU ms
per frame (rex::perf::RecordMainThreadFrame: Xenia from the thread's CPU time between VdSwaps, the Renut from its
"Swap to Swap" time), 1% low over the latest 1000 game frames, and the game frame time graph. debug_overlay_detail =
simple shows only the game FPS; debug_overlay_language = en / pt / es for the labels.

